  "query_preview": "..\nKey Message 1)\nHigh temperatures will be in the 80s in most locations this afternoon\nwith a few spots near 90 degrees. Breezy conditions will continue\ninto the early evening hours.  A cold front will move through on \nFriday ushering in cooler air through the day. Temperatures will then\ngenerally be below normal through at least the middle of next week. \nThere will be the potential that a few spots will have some patchy \nfrost Monday night and then again Tuesday night.\n\nKey Message 2)\nRain showers will start to move into the region late in the overnight\nhours and into the daytime hours on Friday before tapering off. While\nsome locally heavy rainfall will be possible, flooding is not a\nconcern at this time. NBM QPF seemed on the low side given model\nconsensus on higher values and therefore increased QPF for the \nevent. Instability is limited and therefore while some rumbles of\nthunder will be possible, do not expect widespread thunderstorms. Generally\ndry conditions are expected the remainder of the week after Friday.",
